{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community","id":1162077,"title":"How Do You Determine the Local Spirit Community?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-23T20:32:39-08:00","id":1162077,"title":"How Do You Determine the Local Spirit Community?","content":"As the player of a Spirit mage, I recently inflicted a rather hefty narrative dilemma upon my Storyteller, one that I (were I in her place) wouldn't have known how to handle: An emergency &quot;no holds barred&quot; casting of Spirit Summons with eight Reach, calling up to forty spirits of Rank 4 or lower, commanding them to protect an NPC, with a duration of one week and setting the Open Condition on an area the size of a shopping mall. The limitations, of course, being sensory range and the fact that I didn't spend a ninth Reach to summon across the Gauntlet (so only spirits in Twilight would respond).<br /> <br /> Without demanding that the Storyteller have a clear understanding of the spirit ecology in every possible location us itinerant mages might find ourselves, are there any guidelines to suggest how many spirits would respond, how powerful they would be, and the efficacy of their Numina, Influences, and Manifestations in such a situation? (Obviously, I'm under no delusion that anywhere near forty spirits would respond... but at the same time, I have absolutely no idea if the number should be &quot;zero&quot; or &quot;thirty-nine&quot; or any idea whatsoever in between!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T03:56:43-08:00","id":1162137,"title":"","content":"I would probably do something like Rank 1 x 5, Rank 2 x 3, Rank 3 x 2, Rank 4 x 1 = 11 Spirits. Then I would work backwards based on the Resonance of the area. Most powerful resonance has the Rank 4 Spirit etc.... That's assuming there could even be a Rank 4 Spirit given the area. The example in the book of such a Spirit is &quot;The spirit of a city\u2019s principal river&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm new at Spirits, but I would also likely keep in mind that most of them probably feed on different types of Resonance. If two Spirits of different Rank want the same Resonance, it's fairly likely that the higher Rank Spirit would consume the lower ranked one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-24-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T07:34:39-08:00","id":1162172,"title":"","content":"Imo, this is one of those things that\u2019s heavily up to ST fiat, but I\u2019d keep in mind that spirits in Twilight are pretty rare and I\u2019d also take into account the strength of the Gauntlet and if any Verges are within the area of the spell as a context factor for how many spirits might have managed to leave the Shadow and exist in Twilight locally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T10:34:32-08:00","id":1162214,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The numbers I quoted were high. Even one of Rank 1-3 for a total of 3 would be a decent number on this side of the Gauntlet from what people have been suggesting lately.<br /> <br /> But this might be something we can give some suggested mechanics to help STs, so here's my stab at it:<br /> <br /> Total Ranks = 5 + 5*(# of Loci/Verges) - Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> Distribution of Ranks -&gt; Rank 1 - 50%, Rank 2 - 30%, Rank 3 - 15%, Rank 4 - 5%<br /> <br /> Then you have something to go on that you can use ST fiat to tweak up or down depending on the story and circumstances.<br /> <br /> So a dense urban area with no Loci/Verges has nothing on this side of the Gauntlet. Whereas a Wilderness containing a Verge might have 8 Ranks worth of spirits (4 Rank 1, 2 Rank 2, 1 Rank 2 or 3).<br /> <br /> It's just a guideline when you're in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-24-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T21:19:59-08:00","id":1162347,"title":"","content":"Yeah it depends on the setting. If no one considers the local area to have a spirit problem, you'd be lucky to even get a single rank 2 spirit. However, in my setting that would be an apocalyptic amount of magic because my setting has more spirits invading the physical world than any mages or werewolves can deal with. Beshilu problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T22:55:14-08:00","id":1162366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162214#post1162214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this might be something we can give some suggested mechanics to help STs, so here's my stab at it:<br /> <br /> Total Ranks = 5 + 5*(# of Loci/Verges) - Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> Distribution of Ranks -&gt; Rank 1 - 50%, Rank 2 - 30%, Rank 3 - 15%, Rank 4 - 5%<br /> <br /> Then you have something to go on that you can use ST fiat to tweak up or down depending on the story and circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the sort of thing I'd be looking for. <br /> <br /> What does everyone else think of this as a general &quot;metric&quot; for a conventional World of Darkness setting?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T04:57:22-08:00","id":1162434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162366#post1162366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly the sort of thing I'd be looking for.<br /> <br /> What does everyone else think of this as a general &quot;metric&quot; for a conventional World of Darkness setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Far too much. Unless there is a spirit infestation for one reason or another a regular shopping mall might have one, maybe two spirits in twilight. Or maybe none. Spirits in twilight are not that common.<br /> <br /> Also just fyi: A spirit who'd be compelled by the spell to act against its nature (including specifically abandoning a manifestation such as a fetter) would get a clash of wills against the spell I'd think. Of course if you use the raw dicepools for spirit clashes that is not as much of an issue as they are a joke.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T06:08:29-08:00","id":1162446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162172#post1162172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo, this is one of those things that\u2019s heavily up to ST fiat, but I\u2019d keep in mind that spirits in Twilight are pretty rare and I\u2019d also take into account the strength of the Gauntlet and if any Verges are within the area of the spell as a context factor for how many spirits might have managed to leave the Shadow and exist in Twilight locally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, you know what type of spirit are regularly on twilight? Those urging people, if not outright possessing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T10:35:14-08:00","id":1162501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community#post1162077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the player of a Spirit mage, I recently inflicted a rather hefty narrative dilemma upon my Storyteller, one that I (were I in her place) wouldn't have known how to handle: An emergency &quot;no holds barred&quot; casting of Spirit Summons with eight Reach, calling up to forty spirits of Rank 4 or lower, commanding them to protect an NPC, with a duration of one week and setting the Open Condition on an area the size of a shopping mall. The limitations, of course, being <b>sensory range</b> and the fact that I didn't spend a ninth Reach to summon across the Gauntlet <b>(so only spirits in Twilight would respond)</b>.<br /> <br /> Without demanding that the Storyteller have a clear understanding of the spirit ecology in every possible location us itinerant mages might find ourselves, are there any guidelines to suggest how many spirits would respond, how powerful they would be, and the efficacy of their Numina, Influences, and Manifestations in such a situation? (Obviously, I'm under no delusion that anywhere near forty spirits would respond... but at the same time, I have absolutely no idea if the number should be &quot;zero&quot; or &quot;thirty-nine&quot; or any idea whatsoever in between!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on if the area has Forsaken werewolves, Pure werewolves, or a combination between the those two groups that will strongly determine if any or how many spirits are on material world side of the Gauntlet. Did the mage bother to look first? Because since it is sensory range the spell should summon exactly how many spirits he sees, hears, and possibly touches, period. Possibly he was hearing some car spirits in traffic he'd assumed were physical cars, perhaps he sees a person who is spirit fettered or possessed without realizing, likely an addiction spirit that looks like the smoke from their ever present cigarette. Barring him sensing spirits he was unaware of, he summons nothing. I'd give the character an occult roll to figure out the reason he summoned nothing if the summoning was an impulsive action or done without plan, otherwise I'd give him an occult roll before even casting the spell to realize sensory summoning spells only summon what you can sense.<br /> <br /> As a side note:<br /> Succeeding so that many spirits within twilight gather around a target is a great way to ensure if there is a werewolf pack in the area they will investigate and likely call a Sacred Hunt on all those spirits AND the reason they are seemingly invading the physical world... Likely the person being protected will be part of that Sacred Hunt, I mean picture it from the Uratha's point of view, you'd likely assume that person was bringing the spirits through and there is a lot of Hunt now, question later mentality in many packs. I mean imagine what a PC pack would do, it's terrible for the person so &quot;protected&quot;... Likely for the summoner too because the hisil is full of snitches peering through the Gauntlet. So it'd be in the mage's best interest if the number wasn't significantly or threateningly large as to escape the notice of the predators which stalk the spirit world and its boundary. Also besides werewolves there are spirits more powerful than rank 4 on the hisil side of things and they pose their own danger when affecting their courts/supply-lines/food-chains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-25-2017, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T13:35:31-08:00","id":1162541,"title":"","content":"Werewolves only matter if you\u2019re doing crossover. Inside the game line of Mage they\u2019re not a consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T19:25:31-08:00","id":1162598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162541#post1162541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves only matter if you\u2019re doing crossover. Inside the game line of Mage they\u2019re not a consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? I've never played a crossover campaign but other splats are always present and contribute to the setting and sometimes the story. Mage is a part of the Chronicles of Darkness, so is other splats. So if you choose to have them there, they make perfect sense, it's even considered the default. If they are not a part of the chronicle, then that's fine as well, but surely it's a more mage-centric world, lacking some elements considered &quot;canon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T19:27:12-08:00","id":1162599,"title":"","content":"Regarding the precautions or preparation taken by my character: No, none at all. This was an emergency situation that was very much desperate (and resulted in a huge Paradox roll and Wisdom loss). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162434#post1162434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far too much. Unless there is a spirit infestation for one reason or another a regular shopping mall might have one, maybe two spirits in twilight. Or maybe none. Spirits in twilight are not that common.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be in line with Johnny Awesome's formula. Absent places of power, the number of available Ranks is 5 - Gauntlet Strength, or 2 Ranks, total, in the area I cast the spell. And I'd consider that a maximum number, perhaps subject to another random roll to see what percentage of that maximum actually existed.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it does seem like there's a lack of clarity in the rules on the number of spirits that would be in Twilight. The rules mention a few additional motivations (e.g. escaping from predators), but the amount of such spirits is left entirely undefined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162434#post1162434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also just fyi: A spirit who'd be compelled by the spell to act against its nature (including specifically abandoning a manifestation such as a fetter) would get a clash of wills against the spell I'd think. Of course if you use the raw dicepools for spirit clashes that is not as much of an issue as they are a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. (Though given the setting and the nature of the command, I don't think there would have been many for whom the command would have gone against their self-interest.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T19:28:52-08:00","id":1162601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162598#post1162598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I've never played a crossover campaign but other splats are always present and contribute to the setting and sometimes the story. Mage is a part of the Chronicles of Darkness, so is other splats. So if you choose to have them there, they make perfect sense, it's even considered the default. If they are not a part of the chronicle, then that's fine as well, but surely it's a more mage-centric world, lacking some elements considered &quot;canon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I agree with you in principle, this particular game I'm in is a homebrew setting with sweeping changes to mages and the way they relate to the world. So, while there may be werewolves or vampires out there, I kind of doubt it (and if there were, they'd be radically different from typical CoD creatures)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T20:39:08-08:00","id":1162617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162599#post1162599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, it does seem like there's a lack of clarity in the rules on the number of spirits that would be in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a &quot;lack of clarity&quot; on that front because the existing rules are &quot;spirits who haven't got a stable Manifestation Condition to hold onto will generally wind up dragged back across the Gauntlet within the day, and most Manifestation Conditions apart from Fetter are temporary without magical intervention.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless there's a locus or two in that shopping mall, you're most likely to attract spirits who've attached themselves to people and animals, barring some very obvious forms of desperate predation behind the scenes from a Materialized spirit or a body-hopping Possession-fiend (either of which could well be the case, but neither of which is likely to be the assumed default state of a shopping mall in your setting).<br /> <br /> Basically the strongest contender without an established lockout of the concept is that you'd see up to a moderate handful of Jagglings who already haunt the space getting roped into protecting this character within the bounds of the mall, and depending on how important this mall is to the city and the wider world those spirits might pay fealty to the spirit of the mall proper or they might be marauding lords of the shopping season or they might be cast-out fugitives from a neighboring domain trying to scrape together the resources to return to glory. You don't so much need a full ecology as a general understanding of what the specific spirits are and how they might relate to the surrounding setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T02:25:11-08:00","id":1162665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162598#post1162598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why? I've never played a crossover campaign but other splats are always present and contribute to the setting and sometimes the story. Mage is a part of the Chronicles of Darkness, so is other splats. So if you choose to have them there, they make perfect sense, it's even considered the default. If they are not a part of the chronicle, then that's fine as well, but surely it's a more mage-centric world, lacking some elements considered &quot;canon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know there is no &quot;canon&quot; in Cofd, it is up to the storyteller if werewolves would be present or not, as well as any of the other supernatural entities of other gamelines. That doesn't mean you did not have a good point though, if werewolves indeed are present in the game they would be a great concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T03:49:03-08:00","id":1162682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162599#post1162599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This seems to be in line with Johnny Awesome's formula. Absent places of power, the number of available Ranks is 5 - Gauntlet Strength, or 2 Ranks, total, in the area I cast the spell. And I'd consider that a maximum number, perhaps subject to another random roll to see what percentage of that maximum actually existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I didn't see the Gauntlet strength. I guess that number somewhat works out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, it does seem like there's a lack of clarity in the rules on the number of spirits that would be in Twilight. The rules mention a few additional motivations (e.g. escaping from predators), but the amount of such spirits is left entirely undefined. </div> </div> </div>It's just not a topic that needs hard and fast rules, just as there are no ghoul about how many people you are supposed to find in an average coffee shop. The ST has to decide how often spirits cross in his game and then determine from scene to scene how many are present, just like with other NPCS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a good point. (Though given the setting and the nature of the command, I don't think there would have been many for whom the command would have gone against their self-interest.) </div> </div> </div>Abandoning a fetter is against their self interest and Fetter is one of the more common manifestations being employed I'd think. And since they can't move away more than a few yards from a fetter and urging has its limits...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T05:19:15-08:00","id":1162695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162665#post1162665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know there is no &quot;canon&quot; in Cofd, it is up to the storyteller if werewolves would be present or not, as well as any of the other supernatural entities of other gamelines. That doesn't mean you did not have a good point though, if werewolves indeed are present in the game they would be a great concern.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the gamelines in their own setting presumes the other gamelines exist, at least to a simplified extent. This presumption about other supernaturals could be or could be different from exactly how the other Splats are presented in their own gameline, this whould be a ST and table choice, much based on their own premises and knowledge about the other. But there still is a presumtion in Mage that werewolves are spirit boarder guards etc etc. This presumption is what i was talking about in &quot;canon&quot;, with those quotation marks around. I'm not saying it exists a canon story and setting, just some basic presumptions in the tool kit of how the CofD world is presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T10:25:09-08:00","id":1162747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1162695#post1162695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the gamelines in their own setting presumes the other gamelines exist, at least to a simplified extent. This presumption about other supernaturals could be or could be different from exactly how the other Splats are presented in their own gameline, this whould be a ST and table choice, much based on their own premises and knowledge about the other. But there still is a presumtion in Mage that werewolves are spirit boarder guards etc etc. This presumption is what i was talking about in &quot;canon&quot;, with those quotation marks around. I'm not saying it exists a canon story and setting, just some basic presumptions in the tool kit of how the CofD world is presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stereotypes are there for a reason, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:31:55-08:00","id":1163291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community#post1162077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the player of a Spirit mage, I recently inflicted a rather hefty narrative dilemma upon my Storyteller, one that I (were I in her place) wouldn't have known how to handle: An emergency &quot;no holds barred&quot; casting of Spirit Summons with eight Reach, calling up to forty spirits of Rank 4 or lower, commanding them to protect an NPC, with a duration of one week and setting the Open Condition on an area the size of a shopping mall. The limitations, of course, being sensory range and the fact that I didn't spend a ninth Reach to summon across the Gauntlet (so only spirits in Twilight would respond).</div> </div> </div> </div>What time of day did they cast the spell? As others have pointed out, spirits aren't normally in Twilight, so any 'math' in the equation would be like asking 'how many concepts, objects, animals, or other things are here right now that don't belong,' which would be weird to have some sort of statistic for. But during daytime the current flows away from the Hisil, and more spirits are likely to cross then. It's feasible that some might cross just temporarily to avoid daytime. Other things might depend on the mall itself.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I would have a lot of fun with having an entire mall with an Open Condition. From a storyteller perspective it's like Pandora deciding her character opens the box to see what's inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-28-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T20:50:46-08:00","id":1163809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163291#post1163291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so any 'math' in the equation would be like asking 'how many concepts, objects, animals, or other things are here right now that don't belong,' which would be weird to have some sort of statistic for...</div> </div> </div> </div>That, right there, is the very issue! How many conceptual spirits would be here that don't belong? How many objects would be sufficiently divorced from themselves to be relevant? How many animals would reflect a relevant presence in the Shadow... and how many of them would seek to return across the Gauntlet, into Twilight?<br /> Granted: It is <i>entirely </i>within the purview of the Storyteller to answer these questions, and to then use those answers to inform their response to such a potent working of the Spirit Arcanum.<br /> <br /> But... where is the guidance to those Storytellers? There is literally *nothing*, and to me, that seems like an obvious gap that needs to be filled.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":13110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","user":"Eunomiac","date":". 11-29-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:32:01-08:00","id":1163817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163809#post1163809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, right there, is the very issue! How many conceptual spirits would be here that don't belong? How many objects would be sufficiently divorced from themselves to be relevant? How many animals would reflect a relevant presence in the Shadow... and how many of them would seek to return across the Gauntlet, into Twilight?<br /> Granted: It is <i>entirely </i>within the purview of the Storyteller to answer these questions, and to then use those answers to inform their response to such a potent working of the Spirit Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting with the basics, <i>everything </i>has a reflection in the Shadow. But a lot of that is going to be dormant or absorbed into a larger aspect (a sheet might be incorporated into a bed spirit).<br /> <br /> The Shadow is their native habitat, though. They don't belong in the real world. If they come into the real world, they do so in Twilight Form, then potentially Manifest further from there.<br /> <br /> As for what would? Just like humans, you need a few things when it comes to crossing over. Opportunity and means, as not every spirit is powerful enough to get across on its own or has a locus to access. And motive, as a bed spirit is going to be fairly content as long as someone keeps sleeping in its bed, but an anger spirit is out of 'food' once people stop being angry (this is reflected in the books, conceptual spirits are more likely to cross, because their sources of Essence are more fleeting). There's some more complexity to it, as it takes some drive to cross the Gauntlet, more so than just hunger, I think. Spirits risk destruction when entering the real world, and even if they manage to survive it there can be no coming back (simply because that place a spirit thought wasn't enough might be occupied in your absence).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But... where is the guidance to those Storytellers? There is literally *nothing*, and to me, that seems like an obvious gap that needs to be filled. </div> </div> </div>Most of it is in werewolf, as they deal heavily with spirits. There's also the 'blue book' <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Book_of_Spirits\" target=\"_blank\">the Book of Spirits</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T21:40:04-08:00","id":1163820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eunomiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163809#post1163809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... where is the guidance to those Storytellers? There is literally *nothing*, and to me, that seems like an obvious gap that needs to be filled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gap is literally already filled by the facts that these are questions for the Storyteller to answer in this storytelling game that they are notionally acting as a director and mediator for, that a spirit's Rank broadly scales with its significance, and that most spirits that dare to cross the Gauntlet rather than simpy warm themselves at a compatible locus occupy a high-middling stattable Rank rather than the equivalent band occupied in Deathly Twilight by the vast majority of ghosts.<br /> <br /> Spirits that hang around outside of the Shadow are powerful enough to give mortals significant trouble and harried enough by the way reality works that they need a sponsor or an anchor to stay there long-term. The fact that you've targeted <i>a shopping mall</i> and given it an ample buffer of Scale factors softens some of the blow in terms of being able to leave the spell alone, but &quot;call a large number of entities within a limited area without accounting for those entities not usually being outside their home dimension in force&quot; is one of those things that conceptually kneecaps itself no matter how impressive the spell's numerical ratings are unless the ST throws you a bone or you've knowingly leveraged an unusual circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:04:18-08:00","id":1163964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163820#post1163820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gap is literally already filled by the facts that these are questions for the Storyteller to answer in this storytelling game that they are notionally acting as a director and mediator for, that a spirit's Rank broadly scales with its significance, and that most spirits that dare to cross the Gauntlet rather than simpy warm themselves at a compatible locus occupy a high-middling stattable Rank rather than the equivalent band occupied in Deathly Twilight by the vast majority of ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all fine, but the Shadow is repeatedly described as a rich and complex ecosystem, and for it to be effectively portrayed as such in play it has to make some kind sense, that can be hard when Storytellers have to arbitrarily adjudicate basic things like average population density. We don't need census data, but some more guidance of how it is intended to look like would be nice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:32:19-08:00","id":1163974,"title":"","content":"The unfortunate thing is that there isn't a lot of guidance about any of this in the core 2e book. Book of Spirits is worth picking up and should give more to go on. The reality is that Mage is almost unplayable without your ST having access to these forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:38:19-08:00","id":1163977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163974#post1163974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unfortunate thing is that there isn't a lot of guidance about any of this in the core 2e book. Book of Spirits is worth picking up and should give more to go on. The reality is that Mage is almost unplayable without your ST having access to these forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anecdotal evidence says otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:19:57-08:00","id":1163995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163964#post1163964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all fine, but the Shadow is repeatedly described as a rich and complex ecosystem</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritual Twilight is not the Shadow and the degree of richness a given section of the Shadow evinces is a near-direct function of its reflection's history and activity. By default an established domain's ecosystem operates in at least rough symbolic parallel with its roots until some accident or meddling (from outside forces or sufficiently powerful/ambitious spirits) turns some portion of the population's eye toward the less populated side of the Gauntlet. Without knowing more about this shopping mall there is no way to properly speculate on the quality and quantity of spiritual phenomena that can exist comfortably within its walls. The Shadow has always been example-dependent for the &quot;what it looks like&quot; side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:03:50-08:00","id":1164005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162077-how-do-you-determine-the-local-spirit-community?p=1163977#post1163977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anecdotal evidence says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at least one player at the table anyway. We'll leave this topic for another time if you don't mind though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-30-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}